From 3f7a50bf138d78fb687662d1eeac8c016ff9e2ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 2ax4 <2ax4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:22:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Java Edition plays without a Microsoft account
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An offline name (a kept one, or the name the game made up) now plays a
Java instance too: java_player returns the offline player past the owner
gate — the name, vanilla's OfflinePlayer UUID for it, and no token — so
Play no longer opens the Sign in to play screen.

Mojang's game files are public, so the version download no longer stops
at the owner gate either: an owner's name still leads the log, an offline
player gets a plain line, and the error keeps naming the owner when there
is one. The download-for-an-owner-only test now asks for the offline
downloads too, and a new test pins the offline player's name, UUID and
empty token.
